  "folder": "eERQgCFjfeBpm4Pj",
  "sort": 200000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You draw power from the strange and ancient horrors of the land, sprouting unnatural growths such as bloody antlers or putrid fangs, or making your shadow lengthen and twist around you. As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of Favored Enemy to take on a ghastly form, gaining the following benefits for 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition, die, or end the transformation (no action required).</p><p><strong>Ancient Armor.</strong> You gain a +1 bonus to AC, your body wreathed in rotten bark and beastly bristles. The bonus increases to +2 at Ranger level 11.</p><p><strong>Prowling Retribution.</strong> Immediately after a creature you can see within 5 feet of you deals damage to you or one of your allies, you can make an Opportunity Attack against it.</p><p><strong>Unnerving Aura.</strong> When you transform and at the start of each of your later turns, each creature of your choice in a 10-foot Emanation originating from you makes a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, a creature has the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
